Dear Eric,

After pondering for a while we now realize what the join() from thread remark in the code regards.

We suggest this slight clarification:

What about

“// This must be called from the thread that constructed this class (see join).”

->

“// This must be called from the thread that constructed this class (see join).
// Specifically, threadpool.join() will be invoked and for it to work, the threadpool.join()
// call must be made from a thread that is not itself a part of the LibBitcoin threadpool.
// An example of such a thread, is the OS process’ main thread, from which this
// class was created.”

